  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Cephalexin, through its structural and functional similarities to other cephalosporin antibiotics, binds to Alb. This is supported by multiple paths where Cephalexin is linked to Cefotetan and Cefonicid, both of which are structurally related to Cephalexin and share the ability to bind to Alb. The lowest common ancestors across these paths indicate a common pathway involving cephalosporin antibiotics, reinforcing the notion of a shared mechanism of action. The scores from the paths suggest varying degrees of similarity and binding potential, but all paths point to a general relationship between Cephalexin and Alb through the cephalosporin class. The evidence is consistent but not entirely uniform, highlighting the importance of structural and functional similarities in drug-target interactions.",
